'''''Antirrhinum molle''''', the '''dwarf snapdragon''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Plantaginaceae]].<ref name="RHS_1371" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/1371/antirrhinum-molle/details |title=''Antirrhinum molle'' dwarf snapdragon |author=<!--Not stated-->|date=2025 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=15 February 2025 |quote=6 suppliers }}</ref> It is native to northeastern Portugal, the central and eastern [[Pyrenees]], and adjacent areas of northern Spain.<ref name="POWO_799196-1" >{{cite POWO |id=799196-1 |title=''Antirrhinum molle'' L. |access-date=15 February 2025 }}</ref> Available from commercial suppliers, it is a semi{{nbh}}evergreen subshrub reaching {{cvt|15|to|20|cm|0}}, with {{cvt|3|cm}} white to pale pink flowers.<ref name="RHS_1371" />

==Subtaxa==
The following subspecies are accepted:<ref name=" POWO_799196-1" />
*''Antirrhinum molle'' subsp. ''lopesianum'' {{small|(Rothm.) P.Silva}} – northeastern Portugal, northwestern Spain
*''Antirrhinum molle'' subsp. ''molle'' – Pyrenees, northeastern Spain

